course: dictionary
lesson: 10781
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around the word, tells you which meaning the writer means. The word valentine can be a card, a person, or a name.
explain: «A real heart is shaped more like a rounded cone with big tubes coming out of the top; the Valentine heart is only a drawing.» The words «only a drawing» are the clue. Here Valentine heart means the heart shape you see on cards, not a real heart.
explain: «The heart grows stronger with exercise like any muscle, and it looks nothing like the heart on a Valentine's card.» A Valentine's card is a card sent on Valentine's Day. Test your meaning by putting it back into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you are right.
fact: A valentine is a card or small gift sent on Valentine's Day to show love or liking.
fact: A valentine is often sent without a name on it, so it is a secret.
fact: Your valentine is the person you send a card to, or the person you love.
fact: Valentine can also be a name, such as Saint Valentine, a Christian saint.
fact: Names and special days start with a capital letter, such as Valentine's Day and Saint Valentine.
exercise: «She sent me a valentine with no name on it.» What is a valentine in this sentence? | *A card or small gift | A kind of cold drink | A street with tall trees | A saint who lived long ago
exercise: «Max is my valentine this year.» What does valentine mean here? | A card with a heart on it | A school bell | *The person I send a card to, or love | A saint
exercise: In «Saint Valentine was a Christian saint», which word tells you Valentine is a name? | was | Christian | *Saint | a
test: «Mia drew a big red heart for her valentine.» What is her valentine? | A school trip | *The person she sends the card to | A type of bread | A red pencil
test: Which sentence uses valentine as a name? | *Saint Valentine was a Christian saint. | I sent my valentine a red rose. | A card with a heart on it is a valentine. | Valentine's Day is in February.
exam: «Ella sent a secret valentine, and now Sam is her valentine.» In the second use, what does valentine mean? | *The person she loves or sends a card to | A saint | A card | A drawn heart shape
